<title>UK: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>		   27/2/97	 20/2/97	  1/3/96</p>
<p>Gasoline	 475-500	 500-525	 525-500</p>
<p>Naphtha	   75-100		75		50</p>
<p>Gas oil    1,650-1,700	   1,750	   1,700</p>
<p>Fuel oil	     350	     400	     400</p>
<p>Jet kero		25		15		10</p>
<p>Gasoline tankage fell, with outgoing heading into Germany and some cargoes moving on transatlantic routes. Incoming naphtha barges slightly outweighed outgoing parcels, with outgoing volumes headed for Germany's petrochemical industry.</p>
<p>Gas oil barges eased, with arrivals from the former Soviet Union countered by outgoing barges travelling into Germany, Switzerland and Benelux.</p>
<p>Fuel oil tankage fell because of straight-run products into Germany and the bunkering sector. Jet tankage rose because of the arrival of material for gas oil purposes.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7646</p>
